# Line endings are LF in the repository, always.
#
# Without this, a tool that writes files in Windows text mode silently converts
# every \n to \r\n, and the next commit shows a whole-file diff for a one-word
# change — which buries the actual edit and makes review pointless. Git checks
# out LF here too, which every editor on Windows has handled for a decade.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated; collapse it in diffs and reviews rather than scrolling past it.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
